  "method": {
    "sampling": "Median of seven changing coefficient vectors; physical irregular 3D point cloud; fixed unit real wavevectors spanning upper hemisphere; alternating helicity. Shared-core physical sampling operator. Strongest CPU among native fused, prepared fused, cached faer both layouts at 1/4/8/16/32 workers, with separate SciPy/OpenBLAS both-layout thread-grid sanity baseline. GPU round trip includes upload/allocation/synchronization/full output download. Setup costs separate.",
    "adjoint": "Fixed-operator F^H g reuses the forward device allocation. Full field cotangent uploaded, coefficient gradient downloaded. Comparison is cached CPU faer only; no prepared fused CPU adjoint performance claim.",
    "fields": "Median of seven warmed evaluations; points uploaded and full fields downloaded each call. Prepared CPU gets weighted polarizations and exact real-wave shortcut. Best of 16/32 workers selected. JIT/first call reported separately.",
    "pilots": "Files named sampling-* and probe-* retain initial exploratory results. Cartesian sampling pilots are excluded from selected results. Mode-tiled kernel variant was rejected after measured slowdown. Nominal bandwidth is a byte/time estimate, not a hardware counter.",
    "memory": "Reported device byte counts cover explicit logical arrays and omit library workspaces and allocator state. Linux VmHWM includes both CPU layouts and driver staging; not peak production VRAM. Caching is optional and uses more memory than CPU/GPU fused sums.",
    "timing_isolation": "GPU and CPU benchmark windows coordinated with other agents; no competing GPU task observed; normal background host services remained running."
  },
